  "metaDescription": "President Prabowo Subianto announced new teacher training programs, studio facilities for distance learning, and salary reform goals during National Teacher…",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "President Prabowo Subianto plans to send 3,350 teachers abroad for training in 2027 to improve educational competencies.",
    "The government is developing 'Guru Studios' to support distance learning and expand access to quality education.",
    "Proposed reforms include plans for teacher salary increases, the transition of honoraries to PPPK status, and improved certification processes."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "During the 2026 National Teacher Day commemorations, President Prabowo Subianto outlined several initiatives aimed at improving the welfare and quality of Indonesian educators. Key policy proposals include the deployment of 3,350 teachers to nine foreign countries, including Canada and Russia, starting in 2027 for professional development. To address accessibility, the administration is establishing 'Guru Studios' designed to facilitate distance education across the nation. During his address, the President signaled support for increasing teacher compensation and streamlining the transition of honorary teachers into the government's employment framework, specifically the PPPK system. These measures follow recent updates regarding the certification of over 800,000 Ministry of Religious Affairs educators. The government also confirmed the appointment of tens of thousands of honorary staff as part of broader efforts to standardize teacher status and professional standards within the national school system.",
